package com.chaogarden.kindergarten;

import java.util.List;

/** Paraphrased Kindergarten guidance for the mod's real rules, presented as original-style topic pages. */
public final class PrincipalTopics025 {
  public record Topic(String id,String title,List<String> pages){}
  public static final List<Topic> TOPICS=List.of(
      topic("chao","What's Chao?","Chao are small creatures with their own personalities, feelings and abilities. Care for one gently, and let its character develop in the garden.","Chao learn from the food, drives, animal DNA and experiences you give them. Two Chao with the same colour can grow into very different companions."),
      topic("garden","Getting to Chao Garden","Place a Chao Teleporter in your world and walk into its tube. The glass lobby connects the garden and Kindergarten. The central transporter returns you home.","Your original location and game mode are remembered during a visit. If you become stuck in the public rooms, the command /chao return provides an emergency way home."),
      topic("raising","Raising Chao","An egg will eventually hatch by itself. You can hold it gently before placing it, or treat it roughly; the newborn remembers that first experience.","Pet your Chao gently. Offer food when it is hungry and allow it to sleep when tired. Hurting it or repeatedly disturbing its rest damages its happiness.","A newborn crawls. It learns to walk at 50 Run points, swim at 100 Swim points, run at 667 Run points and dash at 1334 Run points. A little Fly training helps with short garden ledges."),
      topic("food","Chao Food","The garden grows fruit for hungry Chao. A Chao holds an offered fruit, considers whether it wants to eat, and takes time to finish it. An unwanted item is thrown back.","Different fruit affects different abilities and needs. Garden trees supply their ordinary fruit; the Black Market introduces more unusual varieties through rotating stock. Hover over a fruit to inspect its benefits."),
      topic("trees","Getting Tree Fruits","Plant a fruit seed on suitable soil with enough room above it. Fruit trees have a real canopy and hanging pods; harvest the ripe pods and leave the tree to grow more.","Most fruit can be made into its matching seed. Mushroom foods have no seeds. Wild Garden Fruit grows in the Overworld, Dark Garden Fruit in the Nether, and Hero Garden Fruit in the Aether when installed. Buy other fruit or seeds from traders."),
      topic("eggs","Chao Eggs","Ordinary eggs are not crafted. Very rarely find an egg in chest loot, or buy a base-colour egg from a Black Market Chao. A normal egg is cheaper and a little easier to discover.","Shiny eggs rotate through the shop one colour at a time. Jewel eggs are exceptionally scarce. Nether and End eggs are found in their corresponding dimensions; mod-themed eggs remain reserved for a later update."),
      topic("training","Animals and Chaos Drives","Enemies have a 5% base-drive drop chance when mob loot is enabled, guaranteed for kills credited to a keeper with a Chao equipped. Drives train Swim, Fly, Run or Power. The Black Market sells all four cheaply without a stock limit.","Animal DNA appears in chest loot and rotating shop stock. Dragon, Unicorn and Phoenix samples are a little less common. Repeated samples gradually add their animal parts; different supported parts can mix."),
      topic("growth","Evolution and Alignment","A child's alignment and first adult type settle in the cocoon. The highest earned Swim, Fly, Run or Power points choose its first type; Stamina is excluded. The latest actual increase among tied abilities wins.","The Hero Run prototype changes gradually before and after the cocoon. An adult keeps its Hero alignment and Run first type. More Run training develops Hero/Run/Run; Power training or losing Run training can reverse that specialization without making the Chao younger.","Biological maturity and specialization are separate. Other forms retain their existing paths: Swim opposes Fly, and Run opposes Power. The original separate Chaos Chao eligibility route is retained."),
      topic("school","Classes and Activities","Speak to the teacher while carrying your Chao. Four students share the classroom. A lesson takes ten minutes at normal server speed, and the offered subject rotates every thirty minutes.","A student cannot leave class early. The lesson continues while its keeper visits elsewhere or logs out, as long as the server runs. Return to the teacher to collect the finished student.","Garden transporters organise your own Chao for races and karate. Place race lines and connected flags to make a course, or assemble a seven-by-seven mat for karate."),
      topic("clothing","Clothes and Toys","A hat or outfit is a gift. The Chao holds it and decides whether to wear it. A good mood improves its chance of accepting; an unwanted gift is thrown back.","Place a toy in the garden and let your Chao choose when to play. A shell hat remembers the egg it came from, including its colour and special surface."),
      topic("companions","Chao Companions","Sneak-right-click your Chao to carry it. With the optional Accessories mod, a healthy baby or adult can occupy your Chao Companion slot. Babies ride on your head or back and grant no benefits.","Adults need their earned Run and Swim unlocks to assist movement; levels scale their bonuses. Power helps in combat. Double jump for true elytra movement: Fly training increases its time limit, and maximum Fly removes that limit.","A defeated equipped Chao rests for one minute. Adults retain their happiness and trained-level penalties; babies keep their stats. All-S Omochao can fly freely and use a boost every five seconds."),
      topic("rebirth","Death and Reincarnation","An ordinary Chao eventually reaches the end of its life. A happy Chao can return in a new egg. Its grades are retained, while each point total keeps ten percent.","Take good care of a rebuilt Omochao too. A happy robot leaves a Robo Heart that can help its next build start with better grades. An unhappy robot leaves one component instead.")
  );
  private PrincipalTopics025(){}
  private static Topic topic(String id,String title,String... pages){return new Topic(id,title,List.of(pages));}
  public static int index(String id){for(int i=0;i<TOPICS.size();i++)if(TOPICS.get(i).id.equals(id))return i;return -1;}
}
